00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:50,000
Captain Corelli's Mandolin is a drama, romance,
war film directed by John Madden.

2
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:34,000
When a fisherman leaves to fight with the Greek army during World War II,
his fiancée falls in love with the local Italian commander.

3
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:18,000
Captain Antonio Corelli, played by Nicolas Cage.

4
00:34:56,000 --> 00:35:02,000
Pelagia, played by Penélope Cruz.

5
00:43:40,000 --> 00:43:46,000
Dr. Iannis, played by John Hurt.

6
00:52:24,000 --> 00:52:30,000
Mandras, played by Christian Bale.

7
01:01:08,000 --> 01:01:14,000
Captain Günther Weber, played by David Morrissey.

8
01:09:52,000 --> 01:09:58,000
Drosoula, played by Irene Papas.

9
01:18:36,000 --> 01:18:42,000
Captain Corelli's Mandolin is a 2001 war film directed by John Madden.

10
01:27:20,000 --> 01:27:26,000
It is based on the 1994 novel Captain Corelli's Mandolin by Louis de Bernières.

11
01:36:04,000 --> 01:36:10,000
The film pays homage to the thousands of Italian soldiers executed at the Massacre of the Acqui Division by German forces in
Cephalonia in September 1943, and to the people of Cephalonia who were killed in the post-war earthquake.

12
01:44:48,000 --> 01:44:54,000
The novel's protagonists are portrayed by actors Nicolas Cage and Penélope Cruz.

13
01:53:32,000 --> 01:53:38,000
The film explores themes of allies, greek island,
mandolin, resistance fighter, greek history.

14
02:02:16,000 --> 02:02:22,000
The tone is emotional.
